{
  "title": "03 — AI discovery and grounded answers",
  "description": "Source-linked interview study tour. Read the highlighted code, then explain it in your own words.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/components/ai/conversation.tsx",
      "line": 21,
      "description": "Start with the chat UI, persisted conversation context and initial prompt handling. Distinguish a user submitting a message from returning to this page through history."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/lib/ai.ts",
      "line": 13,
      "description": "Follow the request contract to the AI endpoint. The UI should not have to know embedding details or model provider credentials."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/modules/ai/ai.service.ts",
      "line": 389,
      "description": "Read the orchestration entry point. Identify request budgets, interpretation, event references, retrieval and response validation. Not every greeting should be treated as a discovery request."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/modules/ai/retrieval-context.ts",
      "line": 15,
      "description": "Conversation history is bounded independently of retrieval. Explain why RAG does not replace memory and why character budgets are not exactly model-token counts."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/modules/ai/model-router.ts",
      "line": 36,
      "description": "These are model profile defaults and environment overrides, not proof of which model every live request used. Explain why routing and bounded retries exist."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/modules/events/events.service.ts",
      "line": 457,
      "description": "Business filters remain authoritative: city, date, price, availability and party size. Semantic similarity is not permission to ignore those constraints."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/modules/ai/semantic-retrieval.service.ts",
      "line": 7,
      "description": "The pretrained MiniLM encoder runs locally through Transformers.js. Embeddings are 384-dimensional normalized vectors, not generated responses."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/modules/ai/semantic-retrieval.service.ts",
      "line": 80,
      "description": "Trace hashes, source timestamps, batches and PostgreSQL array storage. Explain freshness and why a large-scale vector index would be a different design."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/modules/ai/retrieval-context.ts",
      "line": 32,
      "description": "Descriptions, FAQ/policy text and ticket descriptions can become passages with event identity. The relevant TEXT, not just numeric vectors, grounds an answer."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/modules/ai/semantic-retrieval.service.ts",
      "line": 131,
      "description": "Lexical selection and embeddings retrieve bounded evidence. Explain keyword fallback, empty evidence and factuality checks. RAG reduces irrelevant context; it does not guarantee correctness."
    }
  ]
}
